      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Introducing HCP-forming elements lowers dislocation core energy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10894205::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Introducing HCP-forming elements increases lattice distortion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10894205::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "HCP-element microalloying increases the simultaneous presence of screw and edge dislocations.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The altered dislocation cores activate additional slip systems.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10894205::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Additional slip activation produces dynamic strain hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HCP-element alloying will increase ductility relative to VNbMoTaW.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10894205::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will retain a yield strength comparable to or only slightly below that of VNbMoTaW.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial effect exists only within a narrow HCP-element concentration window.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Excess HCP-element concentration can cause phase instability or undesirable secondary phases.",
